      "math_academy_id": "e-12963",
      "problem": "Calculate $(-9 ) \\cdot (-5).$",
      "worked_solution": "We have a product of two negative numbers, $\\color{red}-9$ and ${\\color{red}-5}.$ So the product will be positive:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14146707/assets/19366a03a3e5719f10f55911d6ca814ae0f1f20af0022e887e59f6fc0ef22de5.svg)\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we multiply $9$ and $5$ without any signs: $9 \\cdot 5 = 45.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-9)} \\cdot {\\color{red}(-5)} = {\\color{blue}45}.\n$$",
